description:
User request 2026-10-06: ixdar-app/src/main/java/ixdar/geometry/mesh/data is becoming a dumping ground. It holds 49 top-level classes beside the subpackages load/, ops/, paths/ and representation/, mixing core mesh types with whole features. A first reading of the groups (verify by reading each class and its callers, do not trust names alone):
- core types: GeometryBundle, GeometryBundles, MeshTopology, EdgeKey, EdgeMarks, TriangleBvh, TriangleGeometry, UnionFind, MeshDistance, MeshScale, MeshVertexOffset;
- rings and regions: RingRegions, RingRegionExtraction, RingBundle, RingCandidates, RingCandidateExtractor, BranchCrossSectionRing, RegionExplosion (a view animation, possibly not geometry at all);
- skeleton and limbs: MeshSkeletonExtractor, MeshSkeletonComparator, SkeletonSensitivityAnalyzer, LimbAxis, MeshSegmenter;
- patch decomposition and Morse-Smale: Patch, PatchDecomposition, PatchBoundaryWalker, PatchColors, MorseSmaleComplex, MorseSmaleDecomposer, MscCellAssembly, DiscreteGradient, DiscreteGradientCells, SaddlePointDetector, SemanticPatchDecomposer, CrestLineDetector, PrincipalDirectionField, QuadMeshTopologyHelper;
- surfaces and curves: CoonsEvaluator, CoonsReconstructionError, CharrotGregoryPatchSampler, BezierFit, CurveGeometry, BoundarySnap;
- UV and materials: CornerUvField, CornerUvSplit, MaterialData, MaterialSet;
- misplaced entry points: PatchDecomposerCLI (a CLI in a data package).
Decide the target layout (subpackages of mesh.data, or moves to existing packages such as geometry/mesh/quadlayout, scenes, graphics/render/color for PatchColors), justify it in package-info.java files, and move with no behaviour change. Also check the existing subpackages (paths/ has grown with the ring tool) for the same problem. Keep ARCHITECTURE.md and the generated docs in step (they regenerate on build). Timing: several open worktrees edit classes here (CRAW-45 RingRegions, CRAW-49 shared rings, CRAW-50 connection tool, CRAW-57 ring load time); do the move after those land, in one pass, so no worktree has to replay a mass rename. PatchColors' own hex packing duplicates Color/ColorRGB and can be folded into graphics/render/color as part of this.

PatchColors' consolidation is split out as its own ticket (see the IX ticket 'One colour home'); IX-23 should not move PatchColors separately.

That ticket is IX-24.
